The name is "alex", while the typed is "aaleex".
The namechars is an empty list of text.
The namecounts is an empty list of whole numbers.
For every spot from 0 to the last position of name.
The symbol is the slice of name from spot to spot plus 1.
If spot is 0, Place symbol into namechars, Place 1 into namecounts.
If spot is more than 0.
The prior is the slice of name from spot minus 1 to spot.
If symbol matches prior, The local is the last position of namecounts, set item local of namecounts to item local of namecounts plus 1.
If symbol does not match prior, Place symbol into namechars, Place 1 into namecounts.

The typedchars is an empty list of text.
The typedcounts is an empty list of whole numbers.
For every spot from 0 to the last position of typed.
The symbol is the slice of typed from spot to spot plus 1.
If spot is 0, Place symbol into typedchars, Place 1 into typedcounts.
If spot is more than 0.
The prior is the slice of typed from spot minus 1 to spot.
If symbol matches prior, The local is the last position of typedcounts, set item local of typedcounts to item local of typedcounts plus 1.
If symbol does not match prior, Place symbol into typedchars, Place 1 into typedcounts.

The good is 1.
The namegroups is the number of items in namechars.
The typedgroups is the number of items in typedchars.
If namegroups is not typedgroups, set good to 0.
For every spot from 0 to the last position of namechars.
If item spot of namechars does not match item spot of typedchars, set good to 0.
If item spot of typedcounts is less than item spot of namecounts, set good to 0.

If good is 1, show true, otherwise show false.
